<title>USA: North Carolina House approves spending extension.</title>
<headline>North Carolina House approves spending extension.</headline>
<dateline>RALEIGH, N.C. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Carolina's House of Representatives approved a resolution extending state spending at current levels at least until Aug 1.</p>
<p>The measure was approved unanimously Monday.</p>
<p>The proposal passed in the Senate last week after lawmakers acknowledged the General Assembly would not reach a budget agreement by the start of the new fiscal year on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Leaders of the two chambers said they have moved closer together on their proposed $11.4 billion budgets, but still must resolve a few differences.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
</text>
